IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `roc-core`

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 64: SERVICE OF FOREIGN PROCESS (part roc12, layer 1).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  Every decision function answers `MAYBE BOOLEAN`.
--   JUST TRUE    the thing holds as the Order states it.
--   JUST FALSE   the Order says no in its own words (a flat negative, a "where" or "if" condition
--                that is not met, a closed "means" definition, a period the text fixes).
--   NOTHING      the Order does not answer: it is silent, it limits a grant by its own wording, a
--                bare "must" has not been done (the Order does not say here what follows), or the
--                answer lives in a provision or an Act outside the sources.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Every answer in the Rules carries the caveat of O 3 r 2(1) (the Court's discretion to order otherwise);
-- it is a caveat on all of them and is an input of none (see NOTES.md).
--
-- This Order mostly speaks to officials (the Minister, the Registrar, the process server).  Each such rule
-- is encoded for what it decides; what it means for the person who sent the request is in the seat layer.


-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 64 -- Service of foreign process`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 1 -- definition of this Order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7403 | 1. In this Order, “process” includes a citation.
@ref O 64 r 1 (src:7403)
GIVEN `the document is a citation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 1 a document is process` MEANS
    IF `the document is a citation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“process” includes a citation"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 2 -- service pursuant to a letter of request received by the Minister`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The letter of request is a foreign tribunal's request, sent through the Minister.  Paragraph (1) says when
-- the Rule applies; the later paragraphs say what must be done.  The person served meets this Rule only
-- through the questions of the seat layer.

-- src:7405 | 2. —(1) This Rule applies in relation to the service of any process required in connection with civil proceedings pending before a court or other tribunal of a foreign country where a letter of request from such a tribunal requesting service on a person in Singapore of any such process sent with the letter is received by the Minister and is sent by the Minister to the Supreme Court with an intimation that it is desirable that effect should be given to the request. (2) In order that service of the process may be effected in accordance with this Rule, the letter of request must be accompanied by a translation of the letter in English, 2 copies of the process to be served and 2 copies of the translation of the process in English.
@ref O 64 r 2(1) (src:7405)
GIVEN `the process is required in connection with civil proceedings pending before a court or other tribunal of a foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a letter of request from such a tribunal requests service on a person in Singapore of the process sent with the letter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the letter of request is received by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister sends it to the Supreme Court with an intimation that it is desirable that effect should be given to the request` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 2(1) this Rule applies to the service` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the process is required in connection with civil proceedings pending before a court or other tribunal of a foreign country`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to the service of any process required in connection with civil proceedings pending before a court or other tribunal of a foreign country"
        IF    `a letter of request from such a tribunal requests service on a person in Singapore of the process sent with the letter`
          AND `the letter of request is received by the Minister`
          AND `the Minister sends it to the Supreme Court with an intimation that it is desirable that effect should be given to the request`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a letter of request from such a tribunal requesting service on a person in Singapore of any such process sent with the letter is received by the Minister and is sent by the Minister to the Supreme Court with an intimation that it is desirable that effect should be given to the request"

@ref O 64 r 2(2) (src:7405)
GIVEN `the letter of request is accompanied by a translation of the letter in English` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of copies of the process to be served that accompany the letter of request` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of copies of the translation of the process in English that accompany the letter of request` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 2(2) the letter of request is accompanied as the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF    `the letter of request is accompanied by a translation of the letter in English`
      AND `the number of copies of the process to be served that accompany the letter of request` AT LEAST 2
      AND `the number of copies of the translation of the process in English that accompany the letter of request` AT LEAST 2
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must be accompanied by"; what follows is paragraph (3), where the Minister considers the letter does not comply and must tell the requesting tribunal

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 2(3) -- the Minister tells the requesting tribunal that the letter does not comply`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7406 | (3) Where the Minister considers that the letter of request does not comply with paragraph (1) or (2), the Minister must inform the requesting court or tribunal of — ( a )
-- src:7407 | the non‑compliance; and
-- src:7408 | ( b )
-- src:7409 | the provisions that must be complied with before the request may be further considered.
@ref O 64 r 2(3) (src:7406-7409)
GIVEN `the Minister considers that the letter of request does not comply with paragraph (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 2(3) the duty to inform the requesting court or tribunal arises` MEANS
    IF `the Minister considers that the letter of request does not comply with paragraph (1) or (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Minister considers that the letter of request does not comply with paragraph (1) or (2)"

@ref O 64 r 2(3)(a) and (b) (src:7406-7409)
GIVEN `the Minister considers that the letter of request does not comply with paragraph (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requesting court or tribunal has been informed of the non-compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requesting court or tribunal has been informed of the provisions that must be complied with before the request may be further considered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 2(3) the requesting court or tribunal has been informed as the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the Minister considers that the letter of request does not comply with paragraph (1) or (2)`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty arises only "Where the Minister considers that the letter of request does not comply"; see `o 64 r 2(3) the duty to inform the requesting court or tribunal arises`
    ELSE IF    `the requesting court or tribunal has been informed of the non-compliance`
           AND `the requesting court or tribunal has been informed of the provisions that must be complied with before the request may be further considered`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must inform"; the text does not say what follows if the Minister does not

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 2(4) to (6) -- how service is effected, and substituted service`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7410 | (4) Subject to paragraph (6) and to any written law which provides for the manner in which documents may be served on a body corporate, service of the process must be effected by leaving a copy of it and of the translation with the person to be served.
@ref O 64 r 2(4) (src:7410)
GIVEN `an order for substituted service has been made under paragraph (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a written law provides for the manner in which documents may be served on the body corporate and applies to this service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 2(4) the requirement to leave a copy with the person to be served applies` MEANS
    IF    `an order for substituted service has been made under paragraph (6)`
       OR `a written law provides for the manner in which documents may be served on the body corporate and applies to this service`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to paragraph (6) and to any written law which provides for the manner in which documents may be served on a body corporate"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref O 64 r 2(4) (src:7410)
GIVEN `an order for substituted service has been made under paragraph (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a written law provides for the manner in which documents may be served on the body corporate and applies to this service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the process and of the translation was left with the person to be served` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 2(4) service has been effected by leaving a copy with the person to be served` MEANS
    IF `o 64 r 2(4) the requirement to leave a copy with the person to be served applies` `an order for substituted service has been made under paragraph (6)` `a written law provides for the manner in which documents may be served on the body corporate and applies to this service` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the requirement is "Subject to paragraph (6) and to any written law which provides for the manner in which documents may be served on a body corporate"; see the companion `...applies`
    ELSE IF `a copy of the process and of the translation was left with the person to be served`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must be effected by leaving a copy"; the text does not say here what follows

-- src:7411 | (5) Service must be effected by the process server.
@ref O 64 r 2(5) (src:7411)
GIVEN `service is effected by the process server` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 2(5) service is effected by the process server` MEANS
    IF `service is effected by the process server`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must be effected by the process server"; the text does not say here what follows if someone else serves

-- src:7412 | (6) Where an application in that behalf is made by the Attorney‑General, the Court may make an order for substituted service of the process, and, where such an order is made, service of the process must be effected by taking such steps as the Court may direct to bring the process to the notice of the person to be served.
@ref O 64 r 2(6) (src:7412)
GIVEN `the Attorney-General has made an application in that behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 2(6) the Court may make an order for substituted service` MEANS
    IF `the Attorney-General has made an application in that behalf`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an application in that behalf is made by the Attorney-General"

@ref O 64 r 2(6) (src:7412)
GIVEN `an order for substituted service has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `service is effected by taking the steps the Court directed to bring the process to the notice of the person to be served` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 2(6) service under the order is effected by the steps the Court directs` MEANS
    IF NOT (`an order for substituted service has been made`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty arises only "where such an order is made"
    ELSE IF `service is effected by taking the steps the Court directed to bring the process to the notice of the person to be served`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must be effected by taking such steps"

