§§ `Rule 2(7) to (9) -- after service: the process server files, the Registrar certifies`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7413 | (7) After service of the process has been effected or (if such be the case) attempts to effect service of it have failed, the process server must file a copy of the process, an affidavit made by the person who served, or attempted to serve, the process stating when, where and how that person did or attempted to do so, a copy of that affidavit and a statement of the costs incurred in effecting, or attempting to effect, service.
@ref O 64 r 2(7) (src:7413)
GIVEN `service of the process has been effected` IS A BOOLEAN
      `attempts to effect service of the process have failed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 2(7) the duty of the process server to file arises` MEANS
    IF `service of the process has been effected` OR `attempts to effect service of the process have failed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "After service of the process has been effected or (if such be the case) attempts to effect service of it have failed"

@ref O 64 r 2(7) (src:7413)
GIVEN `service of the process has been effected` IS A BOOLEAN
      `attempts to effect service of the process have failed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the process server has filed a copy of the process` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the process server has filed an affidavit made by the person who served or attempted to serve the process stating when, where and how` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the process server has filed a copy of that affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the process server has filed a statement of the costs incurred in effecting or attempting to effect service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 2(7) the process server has filed what the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF NOT (`service of the process has been effected` OR `attempts to effect service of the process have failed`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty arises only "After service of the process has been effected or ... attempts to effect service of it have failed"
    ELSE IF    `the process server has filed a copy of the process`
           AND `the process server has filed an affidavit made by the person who served or attempted to serve the process stating when, where and how`
           AND `the process server has filed a copy of that affidavit`
           AND `the process server has filed a statement of the costs incurred in effecting or attempting to effect service`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must file"; the text states no deadline and no consequence here

-- The form in which the Registrar's certificate is given.  A form that is only a form is inert; the form's number is not.
-- src:7414 | (8) The Registrar must give a certificate in Form 94 — ( a )
-- src:7415 | identifying the documents annexed to the certificate, that is to say, the letter of request for service, a copy of the process received with the letter and a copy of the affidavit referred to in paragraph (7);
-- src:7416 | ( b )
-- src:7417 | certifying that the method of service of the process and the proof of service are such as are required by these Rules regulating the service of process of that Court in Singapore or, if such be the case, that service of the process could not be effected for the reason specified in the certificate; and
-- src:7418 | ( c )
-- src:7419 | certifying that the cost of effecting, or attempting to effect, service is the amount so specified.
@ref O 64 r 2(8) (src:7414-7419)
`o 64 r 2(8) the form of the certificate` MEANS "94"

@ref O 64 r 2(8)(a) to (c) (src:7414-7419)
GIVEN `the form used` IS A STRING
      `the certificate identifies the documents annexed to it: the letter of request for service, a copy of the process received with the letter and a copy of the affidavit referred to in paragraph (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate certifies that the method of service and the proof of service are such as these Rules require, or that service could not be effected for the reason specified in the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate certifies that the cost of effecting or attempting to effect service is the amount specified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 2(8) the Registrar's certificate is in the form and says what the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF    `the form used` EQUALS `o 64 r 2(8) the form of the certificate`
      AND `the certificate identifies the documents annexed to it: the letter of request for service, a copy of the process received with the letter and a copy of the affidavit referred to in paragraph (7)`
      AND `the certificate certifies that the method of service and the proof of service are such as these Rules require, or that service could not be effected for the reason specified in the certificate`
      AND `the certificate certifies that the cost of effecting or attempting to effect service is the amount specified`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must give a certificate in Form 94"; the text does not say here what follows if it does not

-- src:7420 | (9) The certificate given under paragraph (8) must be sealed with the seal of the Supreme Court for use out of the jurisdiction and must be sent to the Permanent Secretary to the Minister.
@ref O 64 r 2(9) (src:7420)
GIVEN `the certificate is sealed with the seal of the Supreme Court for use out of the jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate is sent to the Permanent Secretary to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 2(9) the certificate is sealed and sent as the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF    `the certificate is sealed with the seal of the Supreme Court for use out of the jurisdiction`
      AND `the certificate is sent to the Permanent Secretary to the Minister`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must be sealed ... and must be sent"

