§§ `Rule 3 -- alternative mode of service of foreign process`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7422 | 3. —(1) Subject to Rule 4, this Rule applies in relation to the service of any process required in connection with civil proceedings pending before a court or other tribunal of a foreign country where Rule 2 does not apply or is not invoked. (2) Service of any such process within Singapore may be effected by a method of service authorised by these Rules for the service of analogous process issued by the Court.
@ref O 64 r 3(1) (src:7422)
GIVEN `the process is required in connection with civil proceedings pending before a court or other tribunal of a foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Rule 2 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Rule 2 is invoked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Rule 4 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 3(1) this Rule applies to the service` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the process is required in connection with civil proceedings pending before a court or other tribunal of a foreign country`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to the service of any process required in connection with civil proceedings pending before a court or other tribunal of a foreign country"
        IF `Rule 2 applies` AND `Rule 2 is invoked`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where Rule 2 does not apply or is not invoked"
        IF `Rule 4 applies`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to Rule 4" gives Rule 4 precedence where they conflict and does not say this Rule is switched off
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:7422 | 3. —(1) Subject to Rule 4, this Rule applies in relation to the service of any process required in connection with civil proceedings pending before a court or other tribunal of a foreign country where Rule 2 does not apply or is not invoked. (2) Service of any such process within Singapore may be effected by a method of service authorised by these Rules for the service of analogous process issued by the Court.
@ref O 64 r 3(2) (src:7422)
GIVEN `o 64 r 3(1) this Rule applies to the service` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the method of service is authorised by these Rules for the service of analogous process issued by the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 3(2) service within Singapore may be effected by the method` MEANS
    IF `o 64 r 3(1) this Rule applies to the service` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the method of service is authorised by these Rules for the service of analogous process issued by the Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a grant ("may be effected by a method of service authorised by these Rules for the service of analogous process") that does not forbid other methods

-- src:7423 | (3) This Rule applies even though the foreign process is expressed to be or includes a command of the foreign sovereign.
@ref O 64 r 3(3) (src:7423)
GIVEN `the foreign process is expressed to be or includes a command of the foreign sovereign` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 3(3) the foreign sovereign's command stops this Rule applying` MEANS
    IF `the foreign process is expressed to be or includes a command of the foreign sovereign`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Rule applies even though the foreign process is expressed to be or includes a command of the foreign sovereign"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph speaks only of a process that is or includes a command

-- src:7424 | (4) This Rule does not apply where Rule 4A applies or is invoked. [S 780/2023 wef 01/12/2023]
@ref O 64 r 3(4) (src:7424)
GIVEN `Rule 4A applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Rule 4A is invoked` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 3(4) this Rule applies where Rule 4A applies or is invoked` MEANS
    IF `Rule 4A applies` OR `Rule 4A is invoked`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Rule does not apply where Rule 4A applies or is invoked"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (4) says nothing when Rule 4A neither applies nor is invoked

-- Hand-gathered answer (option B of ruling E1, guidance only): does Rule 3 apply?  Paragraph (4) first, then paragraph (1).
-- src:7422 | 3. —(1) Subject to Rule 4, this Rule applies in relation to the service of any process required in connection with civil proceedings pending before a court or other tribunal of a foreign country where Rule 2 does not apply or is not invoked. (2) Service of any such process within Singapore may be effected by a method of service authorised by these Rules for the service of analogous process issued by the Court.
