      `Rule 2 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Rule 2 is invoked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Rule 4 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Rule 4A applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Rule 4A is invoked` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 3 this Rule applies to the service` MEANS
    IF `o 64 r 3(4) this Rule applies where Rule 4A applies or is invoked` `Rule 4A applies` `Rule 4A is invoked` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Rule does not apply where Rule 4A applies or is invoked"
    ELSE `o 64 r 3(1) this Rule applies to the service` `the process is required in connection with civil proceedings pending before a court or other tribunal of a foreign country` `Rule 2 applies` `Rule 2 is invoked` `Rule 4 applies`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 4 -- service under a Civil Procedure Convention`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7426 | 4. —(1) This Rule applies in relation to the service of any process or other court document required in connection with civil proceedings instituted in a court or other tribunal of a foreign country, being a country with which there subsists a Civil Procedure Convention (other than the Hague Service Convention as defined in Order 8, Rule 4A(7)) providing for service in Singapore of process or other court document of the tribunals of that country, where a letter of request from a consular or other authority of that country requesting service on a person in Singapore of any such process or other court document sent with the letter is received by the Registrar. [S 780/2023 wef 01/12/2023]
@ref O 64 r 4(1) (src:7426)
GIVEN `the process or other court document is required in connection with civil proceedings instituted in a court or other tribunal of a foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is a Civil Procedure Convention` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is the Hague Service Convention` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the Convention provides for service in Singapore of process or other court document of the tribunals of that country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a letter of request from a consular or other authority of that country requesting service on a person in Singapore of such process or other court document sent with the letter is received by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 4(1) this Rule applies to the service` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the process or other court document is required in connection with civil proceedings instituted in a court or other tribunal of a foreign country`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to the service of any process or other court document required in connection with civil proceedings instituted in a court or other tribunal of a foreign country"
        IF `the instrument is the Hague Service Convention` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(other than the Hague Service Convention as defined in Order 8, Rule 4A(7))" takes the Hague Service Convention out of what this Rule covers; Rule 4A governs it
        IF `the instrument is a Civil Procedure Convention` EQUALS JUST TRUE
          AND `the Convention provides for service in Singapore of process or other court document of the tribunals of that country`
        THEN
            IF `a letter of request from a consular or other authority of that country requesting service on a person in Singapore of such process or other court document sent with the letter is received by the Registrar`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a letter of request from a consular or other authority of that country requesting service on a person in Singapore of any such process or other court document sent with the letter is received by the Registrar"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a country with which there subsists a Civil Procedure Convention ... providing for service in Singapore"; whether the instrument is one is O 1 r 3(1) and the Third Schedule

-- src:7427 | (2) In order that service of the process or other court document may be effected in accordance with this Rule, the letter of request must be accompanied by a copy of a translation of the process or other court document to be served in English. [S 780/2023 wef 01/12/2023]
@ref O 64 r 4(2) (src:7427)
GIVEN `the letter of request is accompanied by a copy of a translation of the process or other court document to be served in English` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 4(2) the letter of request is accompanied as the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF `the letter of request is accompanied by a copy of a translation of the process or other court document to be served in English`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must be accompanied by"; the text does not say here what follows

-- src:7428 | (3) Subject to any written law which provides for the manner in which documents may be served on bodies corporate and to any special provisions of the relevant Civil Procedure Convention, service of the process or other court document must be effected by leaving the original process or other court document or a copy of it, as indicated in the letter of request, and a copy of the translation with the person to be served. [S 780/2023 wef 01/12/2023]
@ref O 64 r 4(3) (src:7428)
