    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to any written law which provides for the manner in which documents may be served on bodies corporate and to any special provisions of the relevant Civil Procedure Convention"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref O 64 r 4(3) (src:7428)
GIVEN `a written law provides for the manner in which documents may be served on the body corporate and applies to this service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant Civil Procedure Convention has special provisions on the manner of service that apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the original process or other court document, or a copy of it as indicated in the letter of request, and a copy of the translation were left with the person to be served` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 4(3) service has been effected by leaving the document and the translation with the person to be served` MEANS
    IF `o 64 r 4(3) the requirement to leave the original or a copy and a copy of the translation with the person to be served applies` `a written law provides for the manner in which documents may be served on the body corporate and applies to this service` `the relevant Civil Procedure Convention has special provisions on the manner of service that apply` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the requirement is "Subject to" a written law and the Convention's special provisions
    ELSE IF `the original process or other court document, or a copy of it as indicated in the letter of request, and a copy of the translation were left with the person to be served`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must be effected by leaving"

-- src:7429 | (4) Service must be effected by the process server.
