GIVEN `service is effected by the process server` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 4(4) service is effected by the process server` MEANS
    IF `service is effected by the process server`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must be effected by the process server"

-- src:7430 | (5) After service of the process or other court document has been effected or (if such be the case) attempts to effect service of it have failed, the process server must file an affidavit made by the person who served, or attempted to serve, the process or other court document stating when, where and how that person did or attempted to do so, and a statement of the costs incurred in effecting, or attempting to effect, service. [S 780/2023 wef 01/12/2023]
@ref O 64 r 4(5) (src:7430)
GIVEN `service of the process or other court document has been effected` IS A BOOLEAN
      `attempts to effect service of the process or other court document have failed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 4(5) the duty of the process server to file an affidavit arises` MEANS
    IF `service of the process or other court document has been effected` OR `attempts to effect service of the process or other court document have failed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "After service of the process or other court document has been effected or (if such be the case) attempts to effect service of it have failed"

@ref O 64 r 4(5) (src:7430)
GIVEN `service of the process or other court document has been effected` IS A BOOLEAN
      `attempts to effect service of the process or other court document have failed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the process server has filed an affidavit made by the person who served or attempted to serve stating when, where and how` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the process server has filed a statement of the costs incurred in effecting or attempting to effect service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 4(5) the process server has filed what the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF NOT (`service of the process or other court document has been effected` OR `attempts to effect service of the process or other court document have failed`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty arises only "After service ... has been effected or ... attempts to effect service of it have failed"
    ELSE IF    `the process server has filed an affidavit made by the person who served or attempted to serve stating when, where and how`
           AND `the process server has filed a statement of the costs incurred in effecting or attempting to effect service`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must file"; no deadline and no consequence stated here

