-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 4A -- service under Article 5 of the Hague Service Convention`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The terms of paragraph (13) come first because the Rule uses them.  "Hague Service Convention" and "Model Form"
-- are given their meaning by Order 8, Rule 4A(7), in another part's range: asked as an input, passed through.

-- src:7474 | (13) In this Rule — “applicant” means the authority or judicial officer competent, under the law of a Contracting State from which a foreign process or other court document originates, to forward a request for service;
-- src:7475 | “Contracting State” means a State (other than Singapore) which is a party to the Hague Service Convention;
-- src:7476 | “Hague Service Convention” has the meaning given by Order 8, Rule 4A(7);
-- src:7477 | “Minister” means the Minister charged with the responsibility for law;
-- src:7478 | “Model Form” has the meaning given by Order 8, Rule 4A(7).
@ref O 64 r 4A(13) “applicant” (src:7474-7478)
GIVEN `the person is an authority or judicial officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is competent, under the law of a Contracting State from which a foreign process or other court document originates, to forward a request for service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 4A(13) a person is the applicant` MEANS
    IF `the person is an authority or judicial officer` AND `the person is competent, under the law of a Contracting State from which a foreign process or other court document originates, to forward a request for service`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“applicant” means the authority or judicial officer competent, under the law of a Contracting State from which a foreign process or other court document originates, to forward a request for service"

@ref O 64 r 4A(13) “Contracting State” (src:7475)
GIVEN `the State is Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State is a party to the Hague Service Convention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 4A(13) a State is a Contracting State` MEANS
    IF `the State is Singapore`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Contracting State” means a State (other than Singapore) which is a party to the Hague Service Convention"
    ELSE IF `the State is a party to the Hague Service Convention`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Contracting State” means a State (other than Singapore) which is a party to the Hague Service Convention"

@ref O 64 r 4A(13) “Hague Service Convention” (src:7476)
