-- src:7437 | 4A. —(1) This Rule applies in relation to the service under Article 5 of the Hague Service Convention of any process or other court document required in connection with civil proceedings in respect of a civil or commercial matter instituted in a court or tribunal of a Contracting State, on a person in Singapore. (2) If any provision in this Rule is inconsistent with any other provision in this Order, the provision in this Rule prevails to the extent of any inconsistency.
@ref O 64 r 4A(1) (src:7437)
GIVEN `the process or other court document is required in connection with civil proceedings in respect of a civil or commercial matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are instituted in a court or tribunal of a Contracting State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the service is under Article 5 of the Hague Service Convention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the service is on a person in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 4A(1) this Rule applies to the service` MEANS
    IF    `the process or other court document is required in connection with civil proceedings in respect of a civil or commercial matter`
      AND `the proceedings are instituted in a court or tribunal of a Contracting State`
      AND `the service is under Article 5 of the Hague Service Convention`
      AND `the service is on a person in Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to the service under Article 5 of the Hague Service Convention of any process or other court document required in connection with civil proceedings in respect of a civil or commercial matter instituted in a court or tribunal of a Contracting State, on a person in Singapore"

@ref O 64 r 4A(2) (src:7437)
GIVEN `a provision in this Rule is inconsistent with another provision in this Order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 4A(2) the provision in this Rule prevails over the other provision of this Order` MEANS
    IF `a provision in this Rule is inconsistent with another provision in this Order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If any provision in this Rule is inconsistent with any other provision in this Order, the provision in this Rule prevails to the extent of any inconsistency"

