         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must file"

@ref O 64 r 4A(11)(b) (src:7468-7469)
GIVEN `service of the document has been effected` IS A BOOLEAN
      `attempts to effect service of the document have failed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar has given the applicant a certificate in the current version of Part 2 of the Model Form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 4A(11)(b) the Registrar has given the applicant the certificate` MEANS
    IF NOT (`service of the document has been effected` OR `attempts to effect service of the document have failed`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty arises only "After service of the document has been effected or ... attempts to effect service of it have failed"
    ELSE IF `the Registrar has given the applicant a certificate in the current version of Part 2 of the Model Form`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must give the applicant a certificate"

-- src:7470 | (12) The certificate given under paragraph (11)( b ) may be in electronic form and must be — ( a )
-- src:7471 | sealed with the seal of the Supreme Court for use out of jurisdiction; and
-- src:7472 | ( b )
-- src:7473 | sent to the Permanent Secretary to the Minister.
@ref O 64 r 4A(12) (src:7470-7473)
GIVEN `the certificate is in electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 4A(12) the certificate may be in electronic form` MEANS
    IF `the certificate is in electronic form`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a permission ("may be in electronic form") that does not forbid a paper certificate

@ref O 64 r 4A(12)(a) and (b) (src:7470-7473)
GIVEN `the certificate is sealed with the seal of the Supreme Court for use out of jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate is sent to the Permanent Secretary to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 4A(12) the certificate is sealed and sent as the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF    `the certificate is sealed with the seal of the Supreme Court for use out of jurisdiction`
      AND `the certificate is sent to the Permanent Secretary to the Minister`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must be sealed ... and sent"

-- src:7479 | (14) For the purposes of calculating the fees that are required to be paid in respect of effecting service under this Rule, the request for service is treated as made in an action filed in the Supreme Court with a value of up to $1 million. [S 780/2023 wef 01/12/2023]
@ref O 64 r 4A(14) (src:7479)
`o 64 r 4A(14) the value of the action in which the request is treated as made` MEANS 1_000_000

@ref O 64 r 4A(14) (src:7479)
`o 64 r 4A(14) the court system of the action in which the request is treated as made` MEANS `Supreme Court`

@ref O 64 r 4A(14) (src:7479)
GIVEN `the fees are those required to be paid in respect of effecting service under Rule 4A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 4A(14) the request is treated as made in a Supreme Court action of value up to $1 million` MEANS
    IF `the fees are those required to be paid in respect of effecting service under Rule 4A`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of calculating the fees that are required to be paid in respect of effecting service under this Rule"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 5 -- costs of service to be certified by the Registrar`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7481 | 5. A statement of the costs incurred in effecting, or attempting to effect, service under Rule 2 or 4 must be submitted to the Registrar who must certify the amount properly payable in respect of those costs.
@ref O 64 r 5 (src:7481)
GIVEN `the costs are incurred in effecting or attempting to effect service under Rule 2 or 4` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a statement of those costs has been submitted to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 5 the statement of costs has been submitted to the Registrar` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the costs are incurred in effecting or attempting to effect service under Rule 2 or 4`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "incurred in effecting, or attempting to effect, service under Rule 2 or 4" (costs under Rule 4A are paid by the sum in Rule 4A(4)(e))
    ELSE IF `a statement of those costs has been submitted to the Registrar`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must be submitted"

@ref O 64 r 5 (src:7481)
GIVEN `the costs are incurred in effecting or attempting to effect service under Rule 2 or 4` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar has certified the amount properly payable in respect of those costs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 64 r 5 the Registrar has certified the amount properly payable` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the costs are incurred in effecting or attempting to effect service under Rule 2 or 4`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "under Rule 2 or 4"
    ELSE IF `the Registrar has certified the amount properly payable in respect of those costs`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must certify"

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 64 -- the duties as regulative rules`
-- ===========================================================================

-- The text names who must act (the Minister, the process server, the Registrar) and states no deadline for
-- any duty in this Order, so no rule below has a WITHIN: with no deadline a duty can be left standing but
-- cannot lapse.  What the text says follows non-compliance is in the decision functions above (for example
-- paragraph (3) follows paragraph (2)); the BREACH reasons here say only that the stated duty was not done.
-- Each rule is run with #TRACE below; the outcome of each run is recorded in NOTES.md.

DECLARE `o 64 party` IS ONE OF
    `o 64 the Minister`
    `o 64 the process server`
    `o 64 the Registrar`

DECLARE `o 64 act` IS ONE OF
    `o 64 inform the requesting tribunal or the applicant`
    `o 64 refuse the request and give the reasons`
    `o 64 forward the request to the Supreme Court`
    `o 64 file the affidavit and the statement of costs`
    `o 64 give the certificate`
    `o 64 seal the certificate and send it`
    `o 64 certify the amount properly payable`

-- src:7406 | (3) Where the Minister considers that the letter of request does not comply with paragraph (1) or (2), the Minister must inform the requesting court or tribunal of — ( a )
-- src:7407 | the non‑compliance; and
-- src:7408 | ( b )
-- src:7409 | the provisions that must be complied with before the request may be further considered.
@ref O 64 r 2(3) (src:7406-7409)
`o 64 r 2(3) the Minister's duty to inform the requesting tribunal` MEANS
    PARTY `o 64 the Minister`
    MUST `o 64 inform the requesting tribunal or the applicant`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 64 the Minister` BECAUSE "the Minister did not inform the requesting court or tribunal of the non-compliance and of the provisions to be complied with"

-- src:7413 | (7) After service of the process has been effected or (if such be the case) attempts to effect service of it have failed, the process server must file a copy of the process, an affidavit made by the person who served, or attempted to serve, the process stating when, where and how that person did or attempted to do so, a copy of that affidavit and a statement of the costs incurred in effecting, or attempting to effect, service.
@ref O 64 r 2(7) (src:7413)
`o 64 r 2(7) the process server's duty to file` MEANS
    PARTY `o 64 the process server`
    MUST `o 64 file the affidavit and the statement of costs`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 64 the process server` BECAUSE "the process server did not file the copy of the process, the affidavit, the copy of the affidavit and the statement of costs"

-- src:7414 | (8) The Registrar must give a certificate in Form 94 — ( a )
-- src:7415 | identifying the documents annexed to the certificate, that is to say, the letter of request for service, a copy of the process received with the letter and a copy of the affidavit referred to in paragraph (7);
-- src:7416 | ( b )
-- src:7417 | certifying that the method of service of the process and the proof of service are such as are required by these Rules regulating the service of process of that Court in Singapore or, if such be the case, that service of the process could not be effected for the reason specified in the certificate; and
-- src:7418 | ( c )
-- src:7419 | certifying that the cost of effecting, or attempting to effect, service is the amount so specified.
@ref O 64 r 2(8) (src:7414-7419)
`o 64 r 2(8) the Registrar's duty to give the certificate` MEANS
    PARTY `o 64 the Registrar`
    MUST `o 64 give the certificate`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 64 the Registrar` BECAUSE "the Registrar did not give a certificate in Form 94"

-- src:7420 | (9) The certificate given under paragraph (8) must be sealed with the seal of the Supreme Court for use out of the jurisdiction and must be sent to the Permanent Secretary to the Minister.
@ref O 64 r 2(9) (src:7420)
`o 64 r 2(9) the Registrar's duty to seal and send the certificate` MEANS
    PARTY `o 64 the Registrar`
    MUST `o 64 seal the certificate and send it`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 64 the Registrar` BECAUSE "the certificate was not sealed and sent to the Permanent Secretary to the Minister"

-- src:7450 | (6) Where the Minister considers that the request does not comply with paragraph (3) or (4) or the provisions of the Hague Service Convention, the Minister must inform the applicant of — ( a )
-- src:7451 | the non-compliance; and
-- src:7452 | ( b )
-- src:7453 | the provisions that must be complied with before the request may be further considered.
@ref O 64 r 4A(6) (src:7450-7453)
`o 64 r 4A(6) the Minister's duty to inform the applicant` MEANS
    PARTY `o 64 the Minister`
    MUST `o 64 inform the requesting tribunal or the applicant`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 64 the Minister` BECAUSE "the Minister did not inform the applicant of the non-compliance and of the provisions to be complied with"

-- src:7454 | (7) Where the Minister considers that compliance with the request may infringe the sovereignty or security of Singapore, the Minister may refuse to comply with the request and must — ( a )
-- src:7455 | inform the applicant of the refusal; and
-- src:7456 | ( b )
-- src:7457 | state the reasons for the refusal.
@ref O 64 r 4A(7) (src:7454-7457)
`o 64 r 4A(7) the Minister's duty on refusing the request` MEANS
    PARTY `o 64 the Minister`
    MUST `o 64 refuse the request and give the reasons`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 64 the Minister` BECAUSE "the Minister who refused did not inform the applicant of the refusal and state the reasons"

-- src:7458 | (8) Subject to paragraph (7), where the Minister is satisfied that the request complies with paragraphs (3) and (4) and the provisions of the Hague Service Convention, the Minister must forward the request to the Supreme Court with an intimation that it is desirable that effect should be given to the request.
@ref O 64 r 4A(8) (src:7458)
`o 64 r 4A(8) the Minister's duty to forward the request` MEANS
    PARTY `o 64 the Minister`
    MUST `o 64 forward the request to the Supreme Court`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 64 the Minister` BECAUSE "the Minister did not forward the request to the Supreme Court with an intimation that it is desirable that effect should be given to the request"

-- src:7466 | (11) After service of the document has been effected or (if such be the case) attempts to effect service of it have failed — ( a )
-- src:7467 | the process server must file an affidavit made by the person who served, or attempted to serve, the document stating when, where and how that person did or attempted to do so; and
@ref O 64 r 4A(11)(a) (src:7466-7467)
`o 64 r 4A(11)(a) the process server's duty to file the affidavit` MEANS
    PARTY `o 64 the process server`
    MUST `o 64 file the affidavit and the statement of costs`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 64 the process server` BECAUSE "the process server did not file the affidavit"

-- src:7468 | ( b )
-- src:7469 | the Registrar must give the applicant a certificate in the current version of Part 2 of the Model Form.
@ref O 64 r 4A(11)(b) (src:7468-7469)
`o 64 r 4A(11)(b) the Registrar's duty to give the applicant a certificate` MEANS
    PARTY `o 64 the Registrar`
    MUST `o 64 give the certificate`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 64 the Registrar` BECAUSE "the Registrar did not give the applicant a certificate in Part 2 of the Model Form"

-- src:7481 | 5. A statement of the costs incurred in effecting, or attempting to effect, service under Rule 2 or 4 must be submitted to the Registrar who must certify the amount properly payable in respect of those costs.
@ref O 64 r 5 (src:7481)
`o 64 r 5 the Registrar's duty to certify the amount properly payable` MEANS
    PARTY `o 64 the Registrar`
    MUST `o 64 certify the amount properly payable`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 64 the Registrar` BECAUSE "the Registrar did not certify the amount properly payable in respect of the costs"
